  "seed": 18,
  "form_type": "song",
  "notes": "D gong (pentatonic_major = D E F# A B), the standard tuning of the 21-string guzheng and a comfortable gong-mode centre for the guqin and yangqin patches in Arturia Augmented YANGTZE, which ships guqin/yangqin/pipa rather than guzheng. Harmony is open fifths only (power chords), so there is no third-stacking and no functional pull. Modal rotation to yu is done by moving the drone centre to B (V5/ii5) in C_veil rather than by changing mode, because section mode is restricted to the seven church modes. Every section's lead motif variant has a note count that is a multiple of its base motif's, so each cycle lands one complete statement instead of a fragment; rests are explicit slots in the motif. Voices are a fixed prefix list [guzheng, dizi, erhu, pipa] because peer voices map to MIDI channels by position.",
